    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d53">

                <pb facs="0147" n="65" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg65"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.2211/57: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">De Lambert</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-07-28T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 28, 1925—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>25. Your 33, July 21, 11 a.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d53-f1"/> While Department
                    can not issue exequaturs to consular officers holding commissions from an
                    unrecognized regime it would be disposed at the request of the Ecuadoran
                    Legation to permit Consular officers appointed by the authorities now
                    functioning in Ecuador to carry on their duties provisionally without
                        exequaturs.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d53-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d53-f1" n="11" xml:id="d53-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; the Chargé reported among other matters that the regime in Ecuador
                    had requested him to ascertain if the United States would grant exequaturs to
                    new Ecuadoran consular officers (file No. 822.00/596).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d53-f2" n="12" xml:id="d53-f2-content">
                <p>Subsequently the regime in Ecuador appointed Señor de Ycaza to be consul general
                    at New York, and he was permitted to carry on his duties (file No.
                    702.2211/59).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
